# Contours to 3D mesh

Viking builds 3D surface meshes from 2D annotation contours using the **Bajaj 1996** algorithm (see `MorphologyMesh/Papers/Bajaj96.pdf`). Untiled-region and robustness details follow **Edwards & Bajaj 2011** (`MorphologyMesh/Papers/edwards2011topologically.pdf`).

For full domain context, read the project skill: `.cursor/skills/contours-to-mesh/SKILL.md` (papers summary, code map, debugging workflow).

## Pipeline (do not reorder casually)

`MorphologyGraph` → `SliceGraph` (corresponding vertices) → per-slice `BajajMeshGenerator.GenerateFaces` → `MeshAssemblyPlanner` composite.

Per slice: Delaunay + edge classify → remove invalid → corresponding faces → **close UNTILED** (medial axis) → slice chords (OTV, `Theorem2`/`Theorem4`) → second-pass region cap → end caps + outward normals.

## Edit carefully

- Correspondence at shape intersections is prerequisite for valid tiling; fix `AddPointsAtIntersections` failures before triangulation hacks.
- `TryClosingUntiledRegion` needs cleaned perimeter/interior points before Delaunay.
- Slice-chord tests use progressively loosened `SliceChordTestType` passes — do not delete tests to “fix” one case.
- Preserve volume-coordinate placement; mesh vertices are not mosaic-space.

## Test in MonogameTestbed

`BajajMultiTest` (whole cell), `MeshTest` (repro cases). Log lines `Exception building mesh U: …` come from pass-2 catch in `GenerateFaces`.
